</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Additional Proofs</h2>

<div id="Thmproof2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproof2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof 2</span></span><span id="Thmproof2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 ‣ 4 Theoretical Convergence Analysis ‣ REG: A Regularization Optimizer for Robust Training Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproof2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproof2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Without loss of generality, we assume <math id="Thmproof2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. The proof for the case <math id="Thmproof2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq n</annotation></semantics></math> is analogous, as the Frobenius inner product is symmetric with respect to transposition, i.e., <math id="Thmproof2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle A,B\rangle_{F}=\langle A^{\top},B^{\top}\rangle_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle A,B\rangle_{F}=\langle A^{\top},B^{\top}\rangle_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> for any matrices <math id="Thmproof2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproof2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Step 1. Preliminaries and Key Inequality<span id="Thmproof2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">.
From the <math id="Thmproof2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz continuity of the gradient <math id="Thmproof2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following property, often known as the Descent Lemma:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(Y)\leq f(X)+\langle\nabla f(X),Y-X\rangle_{F}+\frac{L}{2}\|Y-X\|_{F}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(Y)\leq f(X)+\langle\nabla f(X),Y-X\rangle_{F}+\frac{L}{2}\|Y-X\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmproof2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle A,B\rangle_{F}=\mathrm{Tr}(A^{T}B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle A,B\rangle_{F}=\mathrm{Tr}(A^{T}B)</annotation></semantics></math> is the Frobenius inner product.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproof2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproof2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}:=\nabla f(W_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}:=\nabla f(W_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproof2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{G}_{k}:=\mathrm{normal}(G_{k};p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>normal</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{G}_{k}:=\mathrm{normal}(G_{k};p)</annotation></semantics></math>. By substituting the update rule <math id="Thmproof2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k+1}=W_{k}-\alpha\tilde{G}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k+1}=W_{k}-\alpha\tilde{G}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> into this inequality with <math id="Thmproof2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=W_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=W_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproof2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=W_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=W_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and recalling that <math id="Thmproof2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}=\nabla f(W_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}=\nabla f(W_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(W_{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(W_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq f(W_{k})+\langle G_{k},W_{k+1}-W_{k}\rangle_{F}+\frac{L}{2}\|W_{k+1}-W_{k}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq f(W_{k})+\langle G_{k},W_{k+1}-W_{k}\rangle_{F}+\frac{L}{2}\|W_{k+1}-W_{k}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E6Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f(W_{k})-\alpha\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}}{2}\|\tilde{G}_{k}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(W_{k})-\alpha\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}}{2}\|\tilde{G}_{k}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This inequality is central to our proof. The goal is to show that as long as <math id="Thmproof2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the sum of the last two terms on the right-hand side is negative, guaranteeing that <math id="Thmproof2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(W_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(W_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> is a strictly decreasing sequence.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproof2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Step 2. Analysis of the Update Direction <math id="Thmproof2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{G}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{G}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmproof2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">.
By definition, for <math id="Thmproof2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="Thmproof2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th row of <math id="Thmproof2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{G}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{G}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted <math id="Thmproof2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{G}_{k})_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{G}_{k})_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, is:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{G}_{k})_{i}=\frac{(G_{k})_{i}}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{G}_{k})_{i}=\frac{(G_{k})_{i}}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(We adopt the convention that if <math id="Thmproof2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(G_{k})_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(G_{k})_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmproof2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{G}_{k})_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{G}_{k})_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproof2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let’s analyze the inner product term <math id="Thmproof2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and the norm term <math id="Thmproof2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tilde{G}_{k}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tilde{G}_{k}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\langle(G_{k})_{i},(\tilde{G}_{k})_{i}\rangle=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\langle(G_{k})_{i},(G_{k})_{i}\rangle}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\langle(G_{k})_{i},(\tilde{G}_{k})_{i}\rangle=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\langle(G_{k})_{i},(G_{k})_{i}\rangle}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tilde{G}_{k}\|_{F}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\|(\tilde{G}_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tilde{G}_{k}\|_{F}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\|(\tilde{G}_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Provided <math id="Thmproof2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Thmproof2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, which confirms that <math id="Thmproof2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\tilde{G}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\tilde{G}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is a descent direction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproof2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Step 3. Bounding the Key Ratio<span id="Thmproof2.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">.
To ensure convergence, the step size <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> must be chosen carefully. From Eq. equation <a href="#A1.E6" title="In Proof 2 (Proof of Theorem ) ‣ Appendix A Additional Proofs ‣ REG: A Regularization Optimizer for Robust Training Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, the decrease in <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the relationship between <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tilde{G}_{k}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tilde{G}_{k}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us define their ratio as <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{k}=\frac{\|\tilde{G}_{k}\|_{F}^{2}}{\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{m}\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}/\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}^{2}}{\sum_{i=1}^{m}\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}/\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{k}=\frac{\|\tilde{G}_{k}\|_{F}^{2}}{\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{m}\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}/\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}^{2}}{\sum_{i=1}^{m}\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}/\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}=(G_{k})_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}=(G_{k})_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}=\|v_{i}\|_{2}^{2}/\|v_{i}\|_{p}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=\|v_{i}\|_{2}^{2}/\|v_{i}\|_{p}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (for <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>), and <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}=\|v_{i}\|_{2}/\|v_{i}\|_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}=\|v_{i}\|_{2}/\|v_{i}\|_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as a weighted average of the <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{k}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{m}w_{i}z_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{m}w_{i}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{k}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{m}w_{i}z_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{m}w_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Therefore, the value of <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> must lie between the minimum and maximum values of <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\min_{i:(G_{k})_{i}\neq 0}\left(\frac{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}\right)\leq\gamma_{k}\leq\max_{i:(G_{k})_{i}\neq 0}\left(\frac{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{i:(G_{k})_{i}\neq 0}\left(\frac{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}\right)\leq\gamma_{k}\leq\max_{i:(G_{k})_{i}\neq 0}\left(\frac{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the finite-dimensional vector space <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, all norms are equivalent. This means there exist positive constants <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, depending only on the dimension <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and the choice of norm <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for any non-zero vector <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta\leq\frac{\|v\|_{2}}{\|v\|_{p}}\leq\Gamma" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta\leq\frac{\|v\|_{2}}{\|v\|_{p}}\leq\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently, the ratio <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly bounded:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta\leq\gamma_{k}\leq\Gamma" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta\leq\gamma_{k}\leq\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproof2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Step 4. Ensuring Sufficient Decrease in Function Value<span id="Thmproof2.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">.
Rearranging the inequality for <math id="Thmproof2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(W_{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">W</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(W_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math> from Eq. equation <a href="#A1.E6" title="In Proof 2 (Proof of Theorem ) ‣ Appendix A Additional Proofs ‣ REG: A Regularization Optimizer for Robust Training Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(W_{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(W_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq f(W_{k})-\alpha\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}\left(1-\frac{L\alpha}{2}\frac{\|\tilde{G}_{k}\|_{F}^{2}}{\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq f(W_{k})-\alpha\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}\left(1-\frac{L\alpha}{2}\frac{\|\tilde{G}_{k}\|_{F}^{2}}{\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f(W_{k})-\alpha\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}(1-\frac{L\alpha\gamma_{k}}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(W_{k})-\alpha\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}(1-\frac{L\alpha\gamma_{k}}{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">To guarantee a strict decrease in the sequence <math id="Thmproof2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(W_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(W_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, we need the term in the parenthesis to be positive. We select a fixed step size <math id="Thmproof2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies this condition for all possible values of <math id="Thmproof2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="Thmproof2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{k}\leq\Gamma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{k}\leq\Gamma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we must choose <math id="Thmproof2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{L\alpha\Gamma^{2}}{2}&gt;0\implies\alpha&lt;\frac{2}{L\Gamma^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{L\alpha\Gamma^{2}}{2}&gt;0\implies\alpha&lt;\frac{2}{L\Gamma^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let’s choose a step size <math id="Thmproof2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmproof2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\alpha&lt;\frac{2}{L\Gamma^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\alpha&lt;\frac{2}{L\Gamma^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmproof2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=1-\frac{L\alpha\Gamma^{2}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=1-\frac{L\alpha\Gamma^{2}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a positive constant. We then have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(W_{k+1})\leq f(W_{k})-\alpha(1-\frac{L\alpha\gamma_{k}}{2})\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}\leq f(W_{k})-c\alpha\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(W_{k+1})\leq f(W_{k})-\alpha(1-\frac{L\alpha\gamma_{k}}{2})\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}\leq f(W_{k})-c\alpha\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This gives us:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(W_{k})-f(W_{k+1})\geq c\alpha\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(W_{k})-f(W_{k+1})\geq c\alpha\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproof2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Step 5. Proving the Gradient Norm Converges to Zero<span id="Thmproof2.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">.
Summing the above inequality from <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}(f(W_{k})-f(W_{k+1}))\geq c\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}(f(W_{k})-f(W_{k+1}))\geq c\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The left-hand side is a telescoping sum:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(W_{0})-f(W_{N})\geq c\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(W_{0})-f(W_{N})\geq c\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Since <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded below by <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{inf}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{inf}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(W_{N})\geq f_{inf}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(W_{N})\geq f_{inf}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(W_{0})-f_{inf}\geq c\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(W_{0})-f_{inf}\geq c\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">As <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, the left-hand side is a finite constant. The right-hand side is the partial sum of a series with non-negative terms. This implies that the series must converge:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}&lt;\infty" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A necessary condition for a series to converge is that its general term must approach zero. Thus:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{k\to\infty}\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}=\lim_{k\to\infty}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{k\to\infty}\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}=\lim_{k\to\infty}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Now, we use norm equivalence again. There exists a constant <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v\|_{p}\leq\Gamma_{p}\|v\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v\|_{p}\leq\Gamma_{p}\|v\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}\geq\sum_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}}{\Gamma_{p}\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}}=\frac{1}{\Gamma_{p}}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}}{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{p}}\geq\sum_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}}{\Gamma_{p}\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}}=\frac{1}{\Gamma_{p}}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p8.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p8.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Since <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle G_{k},\tilde{G}_{k}\rangle_{F}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> and each term in the sum is non-negative, we must have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{k\to\infty}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{k\to\infty}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p8.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p8.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This further implies that for each <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,m</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{k\to\infty}\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{k\to\infty}\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, the squared Frobenius norm of the entire gradient matrix also tends to zero:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{k\to\infty}\|G_{k}\|_{F}^{2}=\lim_{k\to\infty}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{k\to\infty}\|G_{k}\|_{F}^{2}=\lim_{k\to\infty}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\|(G_{k})_{i}\|_{2}^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof2.p8.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p8.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which means <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{k\to\infty}\|\nabla f(W_{k})\|_{F}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{k\to\infty}\|\nabla f(W_{k})\|_{F}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproof2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have shown that under the given assumptions, the norm of the gradient, <math id="Thmproof2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla f(W_{k})\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla f(W_{k})\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, converges to 0. By definition of a stationary point, this means that if the sequence <math id="Thmproof2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to a point <math id="Thmproof2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmproof2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> must be a stationary point of <math id="Thmproof2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="Thmproof2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f(W^{*})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f(W^{*})=0</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Convergence of Row-Normalized Gradient Descent with Momentum) ‣ 4 Theoretical Convergence Analysis ‣ REG: A Regularization Optimizer for Robust Training Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is tricky. We firstly introduce the auxiliary Lyapunov function. By carefully defining the Lyapunov function, we can prove the final result.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproof3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof 3</span></span><span id="Thmproof3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Convergence of Row-Normalized Gradient Descent with Momentum) ‣ 4 Theoretical Convergence Analysis ‣ REG: A Regularization Optimizer for Robust Training Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproof3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproof3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We define a Lyapunov function <math id="Thmproof3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmproof3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k}=f(W_{k})+c\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k}=f(W_{k})+c\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmproof3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant to be determined later.
By the definition of the <math id="Thmproof3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{normal}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>normal</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{normal}</annotation></semantics></math> operator, for any <math id="Thmproof3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the rows of <math id="Thmproof3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are unit vectors in the <math id="Thmproof3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm. Thus, <math id="Thmproof3.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\|(M_{k})_{i,:}\right\|_{2}^{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|(M_{k})_{i,:}\right\|_{2}^{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmproof3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,m</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that for <math id="Thmproof3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmproof3.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left\|(M_{k})_{i,:}\right\|_{2}^{2}=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left\|(M_{k})_{i,:}\right\|_{2}^{2}=m</annotation></semantics></math>. We initialize with <math id="Thmproof3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{0}=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{0}=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="Thmproof3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|M_{0}\right\|_{F}^{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|M_{0}\right\|_{F}^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproof3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let’s analyze the one-step change in the Lyapunov function for <math id="Thmproof3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k+1}-L_{k}=(f(W_{k+1})-f(W_{k}))+c(\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}-\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k+1}-L_{k}=(f(W_{k+1})-f(W_{k}))+c(\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}-\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">From the <math id="Thmproof3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothness assumption, we have the descent lemma:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(W_{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(W_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq f(W_{k})+\langle\nabla f(W_{k}),W_{k+1}-W_{k}\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\left\|W_{k+1}-W_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq f(W_{k})+\langle\nabla f(W_{k}),W_{k+1}-W_{k}\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\left\|W_{k+1}-W_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f(W_{k})-\alpha\langle\nabla f(W_{k}),M_{k+1}\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\left\|-\alpha M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(W_{k})-\alpha\langle\nabla f(W_{k}),M_{k+1}\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\left\|-\alpha M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f(W_{k})-\alpha\langle\nabla f(W_{k}),M_{k+1}\rangle+\frac{L\alpha^{2}}{2}\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(W_{k})-\alpha\langle\nabla f(W_{k}),M_{k+1}\rangle+\frac{L\alpha^{2}}{2}\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Since <math id="Thmproof3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}=m</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmproof3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, this simplifies to:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(W_{k+1})-f(W_{k})\leq-\alpha\langle\nabla f(W_{k}),M_{k+1}\rangle+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(W_{k+1})-f(W_{k})\leq-\alpha\langle\nabla f(W_{k}),M_{k+1}\rangle+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Substituting this into the Lyapunov difference equation yields:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k+1}-L_{k}\leq-\alpha\langle\nabla f(W_{k}),M_{k+1}\rangle+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}+c(\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}-\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k+1}-L_{k}\leq-\alpha\langle\nabla f(W_{k}),M_{k+1}\rangle+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}+c(\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}-\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The key is to relate the inner product term to quantities we can control. From the algorithm’s definition, we have <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(1-\mu)\nabla f(W_{k})=M^{\prime}_{k+1}-\mu M_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\mu)\nabla f(W_{k})=M^{\prime}_{k+1}-\mu M_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\nabla f(W_{k}),M_{k+1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\nabla f(W_{k}),M_{k+1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\mu}\langle M^{\prime}_{k+1}-\mu M_{k},M_{k+1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\mu}\langle M^{\prime}_{k+1}-\mu M_{k},M_{k+1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\mu}\left(\langle M^{\prime}_{k+1},M_{k+1}\rangle-\mu\langle M_{k},M_{k+1}\rangle\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-\mu}\left(\langle M^{\prime}_{k+1},M_{k+1}\rangle-\mu\langle M_{k},M_{k+1}\rangle\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">By the definition of the normalization,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle M^{\prime}_{k+1},M_{k+1}\rangle=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\langle(M^{\prime}_{k+1})_{i,:},\frac{(M^{\prime}_{k+1})_{i,:}}{\left\|(M^{\prime}_{k+1})_{i,:}\right\|_{2}}\rangle=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left\|(M^{\prime}_{k+1})_{i,:}\right\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle M^{\prime}_{k+1},M_{k+1}\rangle=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\langle(M^{\prime}_{k+1})_{i,:},\frac{(M^{\prime}_{k+1})_{i,:}}{\left\|(M^{\prime}_{k+1})_{i,:}\right\|_{2}}\rangle=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left\|(M^{\prime}_{k+1})_{i,:}\right\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let’s denote this term by <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the second inner product, we use Young’s inequality (<math id="Thmproof3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\langle a,b\rangle\leq\left\|a\right\|_{F}^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\langle a,b\rangle\leq\left\|a\right\|_{F}^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\mu\langle M_{k},M_{k+1}\rangle\geq-\frac{\mu}{2}(\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\mu\langle M_{k},M_{k+1}\rangle\geq-\frac{\mu}{2}(\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Combining these results, we get a lower bound for the inner product:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\nabla f(W_{k}),M_{k+1}\rangle\geq\frac{1}{1-\mu}\left(h_{k}-\frac{\mu}{2}(\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\nabla f(W_{k}),M_{k+1}\rangle\geq\frac{1}{1-\mu}\left(h_{k}-\frac{\mu}{2}(\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Now, substitute this back into (<a href="#A1.E9" title="In Proof 3 (Proof of Theorem ) ‣ Appendix A Additional Proofs ‣ REG: A Regularization Optimizer for Robust Training Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k+1}-L_{k}\leq-\frac{\alpha}{1-\mu}\left(h_{k}-\frac{\mu}{2}(\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2})\right)+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}+c(\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}-\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k+1}-L_{k}\leq-\frac{\alpha}{1-\mu}\left(h_{k}-\frac{\mu}{2}(\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2})\right)+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}+c(\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}-\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Rearranging the terms based on <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k+1}-L_{k}\leq-\frac{\alpha h_{k}}{1-\mu}+\left(\frac{\alpha\mu}{2(1-\mu)}-c\right)\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\left(\frac{\alpha\mu}{2(1-\mu)}+c\right)\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k+1}-L_{k}\leq-\frac{\alpha h_{k}}{1-\mu}+\left(\frac{\alpha\mu}{2(1-\mu)}-c\right)\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\left(\frac{\alpha\mu}{2(1-\mu)}+c\right)\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">To simplify the expression, we choose the constant <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> to eliminate the <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|M_{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> term:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\frac{\alpha\mu}{2(1-\mu)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\frac{\alpha\mu}{2(1-\mu)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Since <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\mu&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\mu&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. With this choice of <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, the inequality becomes:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{k+1}-L_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{k+1}-L_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\frac{\alpha h_{k}}{1-\mu}+\left(\frac{\alpha\mu}{2(1-\mu)}+\frac{\alpha\mu}{2(1-\mu)}\right)\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\frac{\alpha h_{k}}{1-\mu}+\left(\frac{\alpha\mu}{2(1-\mu)}+\frac{\alpha\mu}{2(1-\mu)}\right)\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{\alpha h_{k}}{1-\mu}+\frac{\alpha\mu}{1-\mu}\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{\alpha h_{k}}{1-\mu}+\frac{\alpha\mu}{1-\mu}\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Since <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|M_{k+1}\right\|_{F}^{2}=m</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k+1}-L_{k}\leq-\frac{\alpha h_{k}}{1-\mu}+\frac{\alpha\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k+1}-L_{k}\leq-\frac{\alpha h_{k}}{1-\mu}+\frac{\alpha\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Next, we relate <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{k}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left\|(M^{\prime}_{k+1})_{i,:}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left\|(M^{\prime}_{k+1})_{i,:}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to the gradient norm sum <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g_{k}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left\|(\nabla f(W_{k}))_{i,:}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{k}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left\|(\nabla f(W_{k}))_{i,:}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using the reverse triangle inequality on the sum of row norms:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle h_{k}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left\|(\mu M_{k}+(1-\mu)\nabla f(W_{k}))_{i,:}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{k}=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left\|(\mu M_{k}+(1-\mu)\nabla f(W_{k}))_{i,:}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(\left\|((1-\mu)\nabla f(W_{k}))_{i,:}\right\|_{2}-\left\|(\mu M_{k})_{i,:}\right\|_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(\left\|((1-\mu)\nabla f(W_{k}))_{i,:}\right\|_{2}-\left\|(\mu M_{k})_{i,:}\right\|_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\mu)\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left\|(\nabla f(W_{k}))_{i,:}\right\|_{2}-\mu\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left\|(M_{k})_{i,:}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\mu)\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left\|(\nabla f(W_{k}))_{i,:}\right\|_{2}-\mu\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left\|(M_{k})_{i,:}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\mu)g_{k}-\mu\sum_{i=1}^{m}1=(1-\mu)g_{k}-\mu m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\mu)g_{k}-\mu\sum_{i=1}^{m}1=(1-\mu)g_{k}-\mu m</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Note that for <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{0}=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{0}=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0}\geq(1-\mu)g_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}\geq(1-\mu)g_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. The inequality <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}\geq(1-\mu)g_{k}-\mu m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}\geq(1-\mu)g_{k}-\mu m</annotation></semantics></math> holds for all <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting this lower bound for <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> into (<a href="#A1.E10" title="In Proof 3 (Proof of Theorem ) ‣ Appendix A Additional Proofs ‣ REG: A Regularization Optimizer for Robust Training Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{k+1}-L_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{k+1}-L_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\frac{\alpha}{1-\mu}((1-\mu)g_{k}-\mu m)+\frac{\alpha\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\frac{\alpha}{1-\mu}((1-\mu)g_{k}-\mu m)+\frac{\alpha\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\alpha g_{k}+\frac{\alpha\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{\alpha\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\alpha g_{k}+\frac{\alpha\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{\alpha\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\alpha g_{k}+\frac{2\alpha\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\alpha g_{k}+\frac{2\alpha\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\frac{2\alpha\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\frac{2\alpha\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have the key recursive inequality:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha g_{k}\leq L_{k}-L_{k+1}+C" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha g_{k}\leq L_{k}-L_{k+1}+C</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Summing from <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}g_{k}\leq\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}(L_{k}-L_{k+1})+\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}C=(L_{0}-L_{N})+NC" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}g_{k}\leq\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}(L_{k}-L_{k+1})+\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}C=(L_{0}-L_{N})+NC</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let’s analyze the boundary terms. <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0}=f(W_{0})+c\left\|M_{0}\right\|_{F}^{2}=f(W_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0}=f(W_{0})+c\left\|M_{0}\right\|_{F}^{2}=f(W_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. The Lyapunov function is bounded below because <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{N}=f(W_{N})+c\left\|M_{N}\right\|_{F}^{2}\geq f^{*}+c\cdot 0=f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{N}=f(W_{N})+c\left\|M_{N}\right\|_{F}^{2}\geq f^{*}+c\cdot 0=f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|M_{N}\right\|_{F}^{2}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|M_{N}\right\|_{F}^{2}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>).
Thus, <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0}-L_{N}\leq f(W_{0})-f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0}-L_{N}\leq f(W_{0})-f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}g_{k}\leq f(W_{0})-f^{*}+NC" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}g_{k}\leq f(W_{0})-f^{*}+NC</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Dividing by <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}g_{k}\leq\frac{f(W_{0})-f^{*}}{N\alpha}+\frac{C}{\alpha}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}g_{k}\leq\frac{f(W_{0})-f^{*}}{N\alpha}+\frac{C}{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Since the minimum is less than or equal to the average, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{0\leq k&lt;N}g_{k}\leq\frac{f(W_{0})-f^{*}}{N\alpha}+\frac{1}{\alpha}\left(\frac{2\alpha\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{0\leq k&lt;N}g_{k}\leq\frac{f(W_{0})-f^{*}}{N\alpha}+\frac{1}{\alpha}\left(\frac{2\alpha\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{L\alpha^{2}m}{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{0\leq k&lt;N}g_{k}\leq\frac{f(W_{0})-f^{*}}{N\alpha}+\frac{2\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{L\alpha m}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{0\leq k&lt;N}g_{k}\leq\frac{f(W_{0})-f^{*}}{N\alpha}+\frac{2\mu m}{1-\mu}+\frac{L\alpha m}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Taking the limit as <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, the first term vanishes:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\liminf_{k\to\infty}g_{k}\leq\frac{L\alpha m}{2}+\frac{2\mu m}{1-\mu}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim inf</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\liminf_{k\to\infty}g_{k}\leq\frac{L\alpha m}{2}+\frac{2\mu m}{1-\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This completes the proof.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Distinction from Normalized Gradient Descent</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proposed optimizer is fundamentally distinct from the Normalized Gradient Descent (NGD) algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nesterov, 1984</a>; <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cortés, 2006</a>)</cite>. While the update rule for scalar and vector parameters is identical to that of NGD, a significant divergence emerges when considering higher-dimensional parameters, particularly matrices.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a matrix parameter <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>, the NGD update rule scales the gradient matrix <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f(W)</annotation></semantics></math> by its Frobenius norm, which is equivalent to a global learning rate adjustment. This approach preserves the directional information of the gradient unaltered. In contrast, our proposed optimizer not only modifies the learning rate but also applies a structural transformation to the gradient <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f(W)</annotation></semantics></math> itself. This transformation, which includes both a RACS transformation and a magnitude scaling, results in optimization dynamics that are fundamentally different from those of NGD.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, we conducted an empirical evaluation to compare the performance of NGD under different learning rates on mathematical tasks. The learning rate was initialized with a 5% warm-up and subsequently decayed using a cosine schedule. The results, presented in Table <a href="#A2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix B Distinction from Normalized Gradient Descent ‣ REG: A Regularization Optimizer for Robust Training Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, indicate a strong dependence of NGD on a large learning rate for optimal performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T6" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A2.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A2.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">Datasets</th>
<th id="A2.T6.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">lr=3e-2</th>
<th id="A2.T6.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">lr=3e-3</th>
<th id="A2.T6.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">lr=3e-4</th>
<th id="A2.T6.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">lr=3e-5</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T6.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T6.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">GSM8K (%)</th>
<td id="A2.T6.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">48.4</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A2.T6.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">70.1</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">31.1</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">25.8</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T6.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T6.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">MATH500 (%)</th>
<td id="A2.T6.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">57.4</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A2.T6.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">60.2</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">53.0</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">24.8</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T6.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T6.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">AIME24 (%)</th>
<td id="A2.T6.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">6.7</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">6.7</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A2.T6.2.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">13.3</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">10.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T6.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T6.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">Average (%)</th>
<td id="A2.T6.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">30.8</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A2.T6.2.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">45.7</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">32.4</td>
<td id="A2.T6.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">20.2</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Performance comparison of NGD with different learning rates across mathematical datasets.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Analysis of the training loss revealed that at the large learning rates required for good performance, the loss exhibited minimal or no decrease during the initial training phase. This suggests that NGD is poorly suited for the fine-tuning of pre-trained models. One potential explanation is the high variance in the average magnitude of the NGD updates, which can lead to training instability when compared to optimizers like AdamW and our proposed method.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Specifically, for the update values <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{M}</annotation></semantics></math> in NGD, the RMS of the update is given by:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{RMS}(\tilde{M})^{2}=\frac{1}{mn}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(\frac{M_{ij}}{\|M\|_{F}}\right)^{2}=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>RMS</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{RMS}(\tilde{M})^{2}=\frac{1}{mn}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(\frac{M_{ij}}{\|M\|_{F}}\right)^{2}=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">This implies that the average magnitude for each entry of the matrix is fixed at <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\sqrt{mn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\sqrt{mn}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For LLMs, the parameters of different layers (e.g., embedding layers, attention layers, and MLP layers) possess vastly different scales. This fixed magnitude for updates across varying layer scales makes it challenging for a single learning rate to appropriately adjust all matrix parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, our proposed optimizer rescales the magnitude of each matrix according to its RMS norm and further balances the magnitudes of different channels within a matrix. These operations collectively contribute to a more stable training process. This distinction is particularly significant in the context of Large Language Models, where the vast majority of trainable parameters are represented by matrices. Consequently, the performance of our optimizer is expected to diverge significantly from that of NGD during the training of such models.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Pretraining Experiments</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present the pretraining experiments conducted to evaluate the performance of the proposed regularized optimizer. We trained a Qwen-like model using various optimizers for comparative analysis. The training framework was adapted from the Moonlight repository, accessible at <a href="https://github.com/MoonshotAI/Moonlight" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/MoonshotAI/Moonlight</a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The model architecture is a Qwen2-like configuration with a hidden size of 896, an intermediate size of 4864, 16 attention heads, and 12 hidden layers. The model was trained on the “Elriggs/openwebtext-100k” dataset for one epoch, consistent with the settings specified in the Moonlight framework. The training was performed with a learning rate of 1e-4 and 100 warm-up steps. The progression of the training loss is illustrated in Figure <a href="#A3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Appendix C Pretraining Experiments ‣ REG: A Regularization Optimizer for Robust Training Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.03691v1/figs/combined_loss_curves_fixed_colors.png" id="A3.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:521/348;" width="521" height="348" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Training loss curves for AdamW and the regularized optimizer (REG) on the openwebtext-100k dataset.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As depicted in Figure <a href="#A3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Appendix C Pretraining Experiments ‣ REG: A Regularization Optimizer for Robust Training Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the training losses of the AdamW and the regularized optimizer are notably similar. This observation suggests that the regularized optimizer achieves a competitive performance level with AdamW, despite utilizing only the first momentum term.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>The <span id="A4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">REG</span> Regularization Operator</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this study, the regularization operator, denoted as <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{reg}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>reg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{reg}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, is defined as a normalization procedure applied to the update matrix <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, we employ a single pass of either row-wise or column-wise normalization.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The choice of this simplified operator warrants justification, particularly when contrasted with established practices in numerical analysis. It is common in the numerical analysis literature to iteratively apply row and column normalizations to a matrix to ensure desirable properties, like Ruiz normalization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ruiz, 2001</a>)</cite> or Pock-Chambolle normalization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pock &amp; Chambolle, 2011</a>)</cite>. However, our empirical results from SFT experiments indicate that a single normalization step is sufficient for effective regularization. We observed that applying additional normalization iterations yielded no significant performance gains and could adversely affect the training dynamics. Consequently, we adopt the most straightforward implementation that proved effective.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the sake of completeness, we define a generalized version of the <span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">REG</span> optimizer in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix D The REG Regularization Operator ‣ REG: A Regularization Optimizer for Robust Training Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, which allows for multiple normalization iterations.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> The Generalized <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">REG</span> Optimizer</figcaption>
<p id="alg1.6" class="ltx_p ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom"><span id="alg1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Iteration count for normalization <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, learning rate <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, momentum hyperparameter <math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, norm order <math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in[1,+\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in[1,+\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>, RMS-norm target <math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\mathrm{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>target</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\mathrm{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay <math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break">
<div id="alg1.7" class="ltx_listing ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each training step <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,1,2,\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,1,2,\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text">// Compute update matrix with momentum</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{k+1}\leftarrow\mu M_{k}+(1-\mu)\nabla f(W_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{k+1}\leftarrow\mu M_{k}+(1-\mu)\nabla f(W_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text">// Apply iterative normalization</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{M}\leftarrow M_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{M}\leftarrow M_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,t</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

